# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# By default Pages caches our assets in the browser for hours (e.g. /assets/topbar.js was
# served with max-age=14400), so a deploy wouldn't show up until that window expired or the
# visitor hard-refreshed. For a low-traffic docs site we'd rather have freshness: make the
# browser revalidate with the edge on every load. Responses are still cached, but the browser
# sends a conditional request and gets a cheap 304 when nothing changed — and the new file the
# moment it does.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
